00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:04,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:05,112 --> 00:00:06,470
- Previously…
- You're new here, at least you should learn

2
00:00:06,482 --> 00:00:07,810
how things are done around here.

3
00:00:08,237 --> 00:00:10,290
Since when do you have to be a gangster just to sit in class?

4
00:00:12,253 --> 00:00:14,290
A new bidder competed against us and they got the contract.

5
00:00:14,356 --> 00:00:15,257
Who's that?

6
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:16,321
It's Monchaitrakul.

7
00:00:16,397 --> 00:00:17,970
Why are you talking to me? What do you want?

8
00:00:18,061 --> 00:00:20,650
I saw you working alone, so I came over to keep you company.

9
00:00:20,882 --> 00:00:22,170
I don't want your company.

10
00:00:22,973 --> 00:00:25,090
Can I ask you something? Can we be friends now?

11
00:00:25,090 --> 00:00:27,210
Actually, you don't have to give me your shirt.

12
00:00:27,328 --> 00:00:29,090
How can you wear it when it’s covered in my puke?

13
00:00:29,110 --> 00:00:30,130
[Sinittha Kongpurim]

14
00:00:40,554 --> 00:00:43,130
Anyone who has anything to do with the Monchaitrakul family

15
00:00:43,810 --> 00:00:46,250
- is not allowed to set foot in Kongpurim house.
- [Monchaitrakul]

16
00:00:56,021 --> 00:00:57,022
Hey.

17
00:00:59,112 --> 00:01:00,768
What's with the rush?

18
00:01:06,872 --> 00:01:08,730
We haven't hugged today.

19
00:01:25,370 --> 00:01:26,371
I'm a little tired.

20
00:01:28,482 --> 00:01:29,570
See you in the morning.

21
00:01:39,418 --> 00:01:40,419
Tokyo,

22
00:01:42,960 --> 00:01:43,961
we need to talk.

23
00:01:55,761 --> 00:01:56,762
Have a seat.

24
00:02:00,928 --> 00:02:01,929
What's the matter?

25
00:02:09,620 --> 00:02:12,021
Remember the daughter of that chicken rice vendor at the end of the market?

26
00:02:19,760 --> 00:02:22,250
I went on a date with her the other day.

27
00:02:23,810 --> 00:02:26,906
I booked a whole pool villa and paid for her and all her friends.

28
00:02:27,936 --> 00:02:30,490
Now she won’t reply to my texts or answer my calls.

29
00:02:30,634 --> 00:02:32,010
She might’ve even blocked my number.

30
00:02:34,096 --> 00:02:36,170
It seriously feels like she ghosted me.

31
00:02:36,474 --> 00:02:38,010
Or was she just freeloading off me?

32
00:02:39,720 --> 00:02:40,730
No wonder she ghosted you.

33
00:02:41,530 --> 00:02:44,226
Just look at you. You’re so cringe.

34
00:02:44,354 --> 00:02:46,455
Me? I'm cringe?

35
00:02:48,756 --> 00:02:50,140
Is that all you want to tell me?

36
00:02:50,777 --> 00:02:53,050
Hey, not so fast.

37
00:02:57,386 --> 00:02:59,970
I spilled my secret,

38
00:03:01,402 --> 00:03:02,403
now it's your turn.

39
00:03:05,403 --> 00:03:06,570
You have to spill yours.

40
00:03:09,810 --> 00:03:10,811
That’s our rule, remember?

41
00:03:11,416 --> 00:03:13,010
Secret for secret.

42
00:03:15,430 --> 00:03:16,431
There’s nothing to tell.

43
00:03:18,410 --> 00:03:19,411
Come on, something’s clearly wrong.

44
00:03:20,210 --> 00:03:22,211
I saw you having a serious talk with Dad.

45
00:03:25,510 --> 00:03:27,370
Has someone been picking on you at school?

46
00:03:29,032 --> 00:03:30,033
No.

47
00:03:30,850 --> 00:03:31,851
Are you sure?

48
00:03:36,274 --> 00:03:38,181
Or have you been doing something behind Dad’s back again?

49
00:03:48,010 --> 00:03:49,050
Actually…

50
00:03:50,769 --> 00:03:52,810
I may have snuck into a bar using your name.

51
00:03:54,380 --> 00:03:55,381
I knew it!

52
00:03:56,976 --> 00:03:59,250
And I almost got busted by the cops.

53
00:04:00,210 --> 00:04:03,170
That’s it? Why are you so stressed?

54
00:04:04,510 --> 00:04:05,860
Next time, just tell me.

55
00:04:06,914 --> 00:04:08,810
It’ll be our little secret. I won’t tell Dad.

56
00:04:25,104 --> 00:04:26,105
I feel better now.

57
00:04:47,170 --> 00:04:48,410
[Phakjira Monchaitrakul]

58
00:05:10,110 --> 00:05:12,410
Are you coming to bed yet? The teacher is about to lock the doors.

59
00:05:25,210 --> 00:05:27,250
[Sinittha Kongpurim]

60
00:05:56,280 --> 00:05:57,281
Yi.

61
00:05:57,682 --> 00:05:58,890
- Can I ask you something?
- Yeah.

62
00:05:58,969 --> 00:06:01,390
What did you mean when you said our family’s old enemy had returned?

63
00:06:02,584 --> 00:06:04,410
We’re just stepping on each other’s toes in business, nothing serious.

64
00:06:05,394 --> 00:06:06,395
Oh, yeah?

65
00:06:09,560 --> 00:06:12,061
Those Monchaitrakuls are nothing but merchants

66
00:06:12,328 --> 00:06:13,690
who exploit ordinary people.

67
00:06:14,056 --> 00:06:15,410
But when they realized they couldn’t beat our family,

68
00:06:15,652 --> 00:06:17,330
they all ran back to the provinces with their tails between their legs.

69
00:06:19,670 --> 00:06:20,671
Is that it?

70
00:06:21,010 --> 00:06:23,250
"Tails between their legs"? Are you just making things up now?

71
00:06:25,725 --> 00:06:26,890
You’re still a kid, so stay out of it.

72
00:06:27,117 --> 00:06:29,650
As long as we’re around, you don’t need to worry about any of this.

73
00:06:30,690 --> 00:06:31,691
Push harder.

74
00:06:34,645 --> 00:06:35,810
Why can’t I know?

75
00:06:36,954 --> 00:06:38,410
I’m a Kongpurim too, aren’t I?

76
00:07:05,330 --> 00:07:07,210
[We’re Hiring! Many Openings Available.]

77
00:07:14,410 --> 00:07:17,010
[Join Monchai Construction]

78
00:07:17,060 --> 00:07:18,061
[6-Month Bonus Guaranteed]

79
00:07:24,410 --> 00:07:25,411
Whoa!

80
00:07:26,330 --> 00:07:27,802
Your boyfriend is coming all the way here?

81
00:07:29,333 --> 00:07:30,334
My ex.

82
00:07:31,477 --> 00:07:33,930
Ex-boyfriend or not, who cares? He had the nerve to show up here.

83
00:07:34,429 --> 00:07:37,170
Go take care of it. I’ll be waiting in the cafeteria.

84
00:07:47,010 --> 00:07:48,130
Tong, what are you doing here?

85
00:07:48,744 --> 00:07:51,730
I just want to give you this.

86
00:07:58,552 --> 00:08:01,210
You don’t have to give it back. You can just throw it away.

87
00:08:03,544 --> 00:08:04,610
It probably doesn’t work anymore.

88
00:08:08,530 --> 00:08:09,930
You blocked me on everything.

89
00:08:11,197 --> 00:08:14,450
I just wanted to make sure you were doing okay at your new school.

90
00:08:15,464 --> 00:08:17,290
Is it as good there as when you were with me?

91
00:08:18,390 --> 00:08:20,330
Whether it’s good or not is none of your business.

92
00:08:21,690 --> 00:08:22,691
You should go.

93
00:08:34,258 --> 00:08:35,259
Thanks

94
00:08:36,920 --> 00:08:37,921
for giving it back to me.

95
00:08:40,850 --> 00:08:42,314
Of course I had to return it.

96
00:08:42,581 --> 00:08:44,370
It was a gift from your dad, wasn’t it?

97
00:09:13,658 --> 00:09:15,880
Here’s your shirt back,

98
00:09:17,274 --> 00:09:18,890
freshly washed and softened.

99
00:09:26,090 --> 00:09:28,561
Here is the sweet filling, like I promised.

100
00:09:35,040 --> 00:09:36,041
Thanks.

101
00:09:44,589 --> 00:09:45,590
Hey,

102
00:09:46,232 --> 00:09:47,233
have you done your homework?

103
00:09:48,072 --> 00:09:49,073
Do you want to copy mine?

104
00:09:49,362 --> 00:09:50,570
- Sure.
- Here.

105
00:09:52,850 --> 00:09:53,890
Do you want to have breakfast together?

106
00:09:54,658 --> 00:09:57,370
You’d better hurry, or Paew will eat you alive.

107
00:09:59,250 --> 00:10:00,840
I’m talking to you. Are you even listening?

108
00:10:24,429 --> 00:10:26,850
I saw you hanging around in the library for ages yesterday.

109
00:10:26,930 --> 00:10:28,450
I thought you two had made up.

110
00:10:28,710 --> 00:10:30,770
You had a fight with your new friend?

111
00:10:34,510 --> 00:10:36,410
I don’t even know if I can call her a friend.

112
00:11:01,630 --> 00:11:03,460
They are definitely in cahoots.

113
00:11:06,105 --> 00:11:08,060
We can’t let them disrespect us like this, Dad.

114
00:11:08,624 --> 00:11:10,490
Why don’t I take some men and deal with them once and for all?

115
00:11:11,504 --> 00:11:13,290
Our best move is to strike before they have a chance to prepare.

116
00:11:17,010 --> 00:11:20,770
Why get your own hands dirty when there’s an easier way?

117
00:11:35,650 --> 00:11:38,251
Have you heard? The company building the new port

118
00:11:38,360 --> 00:11:40,090
is going to lay off all the existing workers.

119
00:11:41,373 --> 00:11:43,310
Ing's husband will be laid off, too. Do you know?

120
00:11:44,010 --> 00:11:46,570
If Mr. Po’s broke, who are we going to borrow the money from?

121
00:11:46,930 --> 00:11:49,131
I hate Monchaitrakul. They  started all of this.

122
00:11:50,010 --> 00:11:51,011
Should I start?

123
00:11:52,746 --> 00:11:54,672
Go ahead. What are you waiting for?

124
00:11:57,488 --> 00:11:59,450
Hello, my fellow students.

125
00:11:59,909 --> 00:12:01,738
I'm Phakjira Monchaitrakul.

126
00:12:01,797 --> 00:12:03,310
- Today--
- Are you from Monchaitrakul family?

127
00:13:11,413 --> 00:13:12,650
What the hell is wrong with them?

128
00:13:14,182 --> 00:13:15,182
You didn't know?

129
00:13:20,043 --> 00:13:22,456
Look, Monchaitrakul won the bid for the port project.

130
00:13:24,690 --> 00:13:26,370
[Monchaitrakul Wins Project Contract]

131
00:13:29,485 --> 00:13:30,492
How the hell did that happen?

132
00:13:31,618 --> 00:13:32,690
Dad never said a word.

133
00:13:35,469 --> 00:13:37,170
Isn’t your family the one that’s still here?

134
00:13:38,088 --> 00:13:39,170
They didn't know about this.

135
00:13:39,408 --> 00:13:41,770
No one in my branch of the family uses that surname anymore.

136
00:13:42,117 --> 00:13:45,050
I switched to my mother’s surname years ago, after my father died.

137
00:13:45,866 --> 00:13:47,610
Yours is the only family still using the Monchaitrakul name.

138
00:13:49,481 --> 00:13:50,978
How are things with your classmates?

139
00:13:51,482 --> 00:13:52,910
Tokyo’s in your class too, isn’t she?

140
00:13:55,186 --> 00:13:56,514
That's why she completely ignored me.

141
00:13:58,360 --> 00:13:59,460
I think it was because of this.

142
00:14:00,629 --> 00:14:01,650
You’re acting weird.

143
00:14:02,037 --> 00:14:03,770
Even when Tong didn’t talk to you for a whole week,

144
00:14:03,872 --> 00:14:05,373
you weren’t this upset.

145
00:14:07,717 --> 00:14:10,170
Tokyo’s just a new friend, so why are you making such a big deal out of it?

146
00:14:12,410 --> 00:14:14,490
Honestly, I thought you and Tokyo didn’t even get along.

147
00:14:15,845 --> 00:14:16,846
I don't know.

148
00:14:19,130 --> 00:14:20,290
We're not that close.

149
00:14:25,946 --> 00:14:26,947
I don't care about her.

150
00:14:38,130 --> 00:14:40,731
Well, what a surprise! My daughter finally texted me back.

151
00:14:49,810 --> 00:14:51,650
What’s this about the port concession here?

152
00:15:09,170 --> 00:15:11,171
[FUCK MONCHAITRAKUL]

153
00:15:14,353 --> 00:15:15,570
Lovely artwork on the new desk, don’t you think?

154
00:15:29,354 --> 00:15:30,855
[UGLY AND STUPID]

155
00:15:49,906 --> 00:15:50,907
Tokyo,

156
00:15:52,880 --> 00:15:53,981
I got you.

157
00:16:07,714 --> 00:16:09,515
Hey! What the fuck are you doing?

158
00:16:50,056 --> 00:16:53,210
So, who do you think’s gonna win—

159
00:16:53,362 --> 00:16:54,363
the Monchaitrakuls or the Kongpurims?

160
00:16:56,466 --> 00:16:58,160
We’ll find out who wins soon enough.

161
00:16:58,690 --> 00:17:01,450
Let’s keep it between us at school. Forget the Monchaitrakuls and the Kongpurims.

162
00:17:33,160 --> 00:17:34,490
Where’s my PE shirt?

163
00:17:37,648 --> 00:17:39,808
Whoa! This is harsh.

164
00:17:41,365 --> 00:17:42,810
Damn, these guys don’t mess around.

165
00:17:44,259 --> 00:17:46,860
I’m done taking this shit. Tell me who did it

166
00:17:47,224 --> 00:17:48,370
so I know who to go after.

167
00:17:50,642 --> 00:17:52,050
You’re still trying to act tough, huh?

168
00:17:52,813 --> 00:17:53,814
You’re all alone.

169
00:17:53,960 --> 00:17:56,311
- How are you supposed to take them on?
- You're not helping me?

170
00:17:58,460 --> 00:18:00,210
Count me out. I need to graduate.

171
00:18:00,810 --> 00:18:03,330
I don’t want to spend a third year in 12th grade.

172
00:18:03,760 --> 00:18:06,690
You should stay out of trouble too, especially if you want that university quota.

173
00:18:13,330 --> 00:18:16,370
Just wear your regular school uniform for now. The teacher won’t mind.

174
00:18:46,696 --> 00:18:47,810
Wow. She’s got quite an attitude.

175
00:19:09,872 --> 00:19:10,873
You did it, didn't you?

176
00:19:22,589 --> 00:19:23,610
Gather around.

177
00:19:25,010 --> 00:19:27,170
Class 6/3, line up on this side.

178
00:19:27,805 --> 00:19:29,370
Class 6/8, form a separate line.

179
00:19:29,826 --> 00:19:31,130
Come on, hurry up.

180
00:19:35,232 --> 00:19:37,354
Phakjira? What?

181
00:19:51,434 --> 00:19:52,435
What's got into you?

182
00:19:53,322 --> 00:19:55,770
Can’t you just behave like the rest of your classmates?

183
00:19:56,352 --> 00:19:57,530
You’re always causing trouble.

184
00:19:58,277 --> 00:20:01,290
Then could you ask the others to behave normally too?

185
00:20:07,296 --> 00:20:09,669
If anyone has an issue, we should talk about it face-to-face.

186
00:20:12,368 --> 00:20:13,490
Don’t start.

187
00:20:14,354 --> 00:20:17,443
Is your whole family determined to cause trouble?

188
00:20:17,997 --> 00:20:18,998
I see.

189
00:20:19,592 --> 00:20:20,810
You're one of them, too, right?

190
00:20:20,850 --> 00:20:24,551
If you don’t stop, I’ll deduct points from your conduct score.

191
00:21:26,240 --> 00:21:27,710
Anyone got a problem with Blue?

192
00:21:33,845 --> 00:21:36,392
Come on, let's split into two teams.

193
00:21:36,976 --> 00:21:39,190
Mix the two classes.

194
00:21:39,749 --> 00:21:41,157
Don’t pair up with your own classmates again.

195
00:22:25,210 --> 00:22:26,211
Here.

196
00:22:32,808 --> 00:22:33,809
Here.

197
00:22:34,360 --> 00:22:36,050
That other vendor’s snack wasn’t very good.

198
00:22:36,544 --> 00:22:37,545
This one’s much better.

199
00:22:50,860 --> 00:22:51,861
Yeah.

200
00:23:00,368 --> 00:23:02,090
I thought you'd never talk to me again.

201
00:23:06,880 --> 00:23:08,400
Thanks for sticking up for me in gym class.

202
00:23:10,442 --> 00:23:11,443
Sure.

203
00:23:12,896 --> 00:23:15,650
Honestly, I’m not quite sure how to act around you either.

204
00:23:19,376 --> 00:23:20,377
Do the Kongpurims

205
00:23:21,392 --> 00:23:23,157
really hate the Monchaitrakuls that much?

206
00:23:30,749 --> 00:23:31,750
Yeah.

207
00:23:41,349 --> 00:23:42,350
Honestly,

208
00:23:45,110 --> 00:23:46,930
we shouldn’t even be friends.

209
00:23:57,493 --> 00:23:58,494
Hey.

210
00:24:00,002 --> 00:24:01,703
What did you draw? Let me see.

211
00:24:06,184 --> 00:24:07,185
It's pretty.

212
00:24:09,058 --> 00:24:10,059
I want one, too.

213
00:25:20,805 --> 00:25:21,806
I should get going.

214
00:25:22,458 --> 00:25:23,459
Okay.

215
00:25:39,608 --> 00:25:41,330
I gotta go, see you tomorrow.

216
00:26:03,776 --> 00:26:05,410
People around here really seem to love the Kongpurims.

217
00:26:07,104 --> 00:26:08,810
How have you managed to live here all this time?

218
00:26:10,280 --> 00:26:12,281
My mom’s family keeps to themselves.

219
00:26:12,890 --> 00:26:13,891
You, on the other hand,

220
00:26:14,090 --> 00:26:16,690
just got here and you’re already causing trouble with everyone.

221
00:26:16,834 --> 00:26:18,491
Which side are you on, exactly?

222
00:26:20,150 --> 00:26:21,470
The winning side, of course.

223
00:26:30,762 --> 00:26:33,210
I only came because Mom asked me to.

224
00:26:34,122 --> 00:26:37,210
I don’t get why Dad had to stir up trouble on someone else’s turf.

225
00:26:37,546 --> 00:26:40,690
Come on. Just think of it as checking up on the family business.

226
00:26:42,090 --> 00:26:43,440
That’s what rich kids do.

227
00:26:49,330 --> 00:26:51,890
Get out! Get out! Get out!

228
00:26:52,226 --> 00:26:54,890
Get out! Get out! Get out!

229
00:26:55,925 --> 00:26:56,926
What is it?

230
00:26:57,210 --> 00:26:58,810
Get out! Get out!

231
00:26:59,034 --> 00:27:00,460
Sir, you can park over there.

232
00:27:01,050 --> 00:27:03,690
- Get out! Get out! Get out!
- [We want jobs!]

233
00:27:04,330 --> 00:27:07,810
- Get out! Get out!
- [Monchai Construction—greedy, heartless bloodsuckers!]

234
00:27:08,410 --> 00:27:12,250
- Get out! Get out! Get out!
- [Bad people! Selfish!]

235
00:27:12,682 --> 00:27:15,090
Get out! Get out! Get out!

236
00:27:15,410 --> 00:27:16,411
Get out!

237
00:27:18,045 --> 00:27:19,046
Phu.

238
00:27:28,250 --> 00:27:29,330
Everyone, please calm down.

239
00:27:40,546 --> 00:27:41,547
Here’s what I’ll do:

240
00:27:42,450 --> 00:27:44,730
I’ll pay everyone their final month’s salary,

241
00:27:46,301 --> 00:27:48,090
plus three months’ severance pay.

242
00:27:48,856 --> 00:27:50,890
We don't want it. We want our jobs!

243
00:27:55,400 --> 00:27:58,170
We appreciate the money, but we’d rather keep our jobs.

244
00:27:58,730 --> 00:28:01,050
Exactly! We want to keep our jobs!

245
00:28:01,466 --> 00:28:02,572
We want to keep our jobs!

246
00:28:03,333 --> 00:28:04,570
We want to keep our jobs!

247
00:28:04,960 --> 00:28:06,160
We want to keep our jobs!

248
00:28:06,474 --> 00:28:07,568
Please calm down.

249
00:28:08,362 --> 00:28:11,370
All the workers are being laid off

250
00:28:11,749 --> 00:28:15,280
because the government’s contract with the Kongpurims

251
00:28:15,893 --> 00:28:16,894
has expired.

252
00:28:17,434 --> 00:28:19,040
Monchai Construction

253
00:28:19,730 --> 00:28:22,651
will soon begin recruiting a new workforce,

254
00:28:23,090 --> 00:28:25,930
and every qualified applicant will be considered.

255
00:28:27,210 --> 00:28:30,710
We have only one disqualifying condition:

256
00:28:31,872 --> 00:28:33,059
anyone affiliated with the Kongpurims

257
00:28:33,848 --> 00:28:36,410
will not be hired.

258
00:28:41,290 --> 00:28:42,650
We can't apply then.

259
00:28:46,768 --> 00:28:48,050
How do you know?

260
00:29:13,410 --> 00:29:14,650
How's your new school?

261
00:29:15,250 --> 00:29:16,290
Have you settled in yet?

262
00:29:24,800 --> 00:29:25,801
And…

263
00:29:26,672 --> 00:29:27,750
How’s the dorm?

264
00:29:29,317 --> 00:29:31,650
You don’t have to act interested now, Dad.

265
00:29:32,970 --> 00:29:34,490
You never asked me about anything before.

266
00:29:38,410 --> 00:29:41,570
I want to know why you didn’t tell me you were moving here for the port project.

267
00:29:44,826 --> 00:29:45,827
Well…

268
00:29:46,400 --> 00:29:47,450
It’s grown-up business.

269
00:29:49,557 --> 00:29:53,010
Dad, our business was doing just fine where we were.

270
00:29:54,030 --> 00:29:55,690
We didn’t have any problems, did we?

271
00:29:57,635 --> 00:30:00,330
So why did you have to come here and pick a fight with the local mafia?

272
00:30:08,030 --> 00:30:11,850
You haven’t been hanging around with that Kongpurim kid, have you?

273
00:30:14,560 --> 00:30:16,250
She doesn't even have a friend, Uncle.

274
00:30:19,482 --> 00:30:21,570
She's hanging out with me all the time.

275
00:30:29,770 --> 00:30:32,629
We're not close. We're just in the same class.

276
00:30:37,710 --> 00:30:39,570
Dad, should we have her transferred to a different class?

277
00:30:40,160 --> 00:30:41,161
Are you insane?

278
00:30:42,106 --> 00:30:43,480
Why does she have to move?

279
00:30:44,690 --> 00:30:46,130
You're right.

280
00:30:48,080 --> 00:30:50,010
Then why don’t we get the principal to expel that brat instead?

281
00:30:50,413 --> 00:30:52,221
Come on! Are you stupid or what?

282
00:30:54,810 --> 00:30:56,970
Why don’t we get our little sister to befriend their daughter

283
00:30:57,560 --> 00:30:58,770
and keep her close?

284
00:30:59,730 --> 00:31:01,330
That’ll make things easier for us.

285
00:31:02,424 --> 00:31:04,850
I just don’t want our little sister getting mixed up with the Monchaitrakuls.

286
00:31:05,472 --> 00:31:07,050
- But if it's the only way--
- Hey.

287
00:31:07,834 --> 00:31:09,335
What the hell are you guys planning?

288
00:31:10,128 --> 00:31:12,130
Maybe you should ask what your little sister wants first.

289
00:31:13,850 --> 00:31:14,851
What do you think, honey?

290
00:31:15,760 --> 00:31:18,351
What do you think of the Monchaitrakul girl?

291
00:31:48,082 --> 00:31:50,450
[Singing off-key.]

292
00:32:03,344 --> 00:32:04,970
What is going on with you?

293
00:32:05,608 --> 00:32:07,810
You’ve looked miserable for days.

294
00:32:08,317 --> 00:32:09,610
Yeah, what's wrong?

295
00:32:09,960 --> 00:32:11,970
Are we going to the mo

296
00:32:12,776 --> 00:32:14,472
Are you coming to dorm movie night? Tell me now so I can book the tickets.

297
00:32:14,722 --> 00:32:16,130
Let's go. I want to go.

298
00:32:16,429 --> 00:32:19,090
But don’t get seats too close to the screen. It’ll hurt my neck.

299
00:32:21,053 --> 00:32:23,254
Can you two not talk about movie night right now?

300
00:32:24,344 --> 00:32:25,345
I’m seriously stressed.

301
00:32:26,429 --> 00:32:28,310
What do you have to be stressed about?

302
00:32:29,120 --> 00:32:31,786
You’ve got money, you’re good-looking,

303
00:32:32,250 --> 00:32:33,251
and your family supports you.

304
00:32:35,738 --> 00:32:37,970
I’m stressed because there’s something I want to do,

305
00:32:38,010 --> 00:32:39,610
but I know my family would never approve.

306
00:32:40,150 --> 00:32:41,710
I don’t know what to do.

307
00:32:43,440 --> 00:32:44,441
Well,

308
00:32:45,893 --> 00:32:49,330
then don’t do it.

309
00:32:49,701 --> 00:32:51,371
You’ll always put your family first anyway, right?

310
00:32:51,626 --> 00:32:54,210
Just do whatever your dad and older brother tell you. Problem solved.

311
00:32:55,397 --> 00:32:57,970
She’s stressed because she doesn’t want to do what her family expects.

312
00:32:58,378 --> 00:33:00,710
If she keeps giving in to them, she’ll feel like this for the rest of her life.

313
00:33:01,869 --> 00:33:03,970
Then just…

314
00:33:04,429 --> 00:33:06,370
do it without letting them find out. It’s that simple.

315
00:33:06,669 --> 00:33:08,250
Why are you encouraging her to do that?

316
00:33:08,270 --> 00:33:10,226
If she gets in trouble with her family, are you going to help her?

317
00:33:10,984 --> 00:33:13,370
Oh, do you have a better idea than this?

318
00:33:15,493 --> 00:33:16,494
I don't.

319
00:33:18,224 --> 00:33:19,225
See?

320
00:34:09,490 --> 00:34:11,190
[You kept me waiting forever. I missed you, you know.]

321
00:34:11,210 --> 00:34:12,710
[I missed you too, so I came rushing back to you.]

322
00:34:12,730 --> 00:34:13,811
[Then let’s get some food ready and celebrate.]

323
00:35:05,253 --> 00:35:06,570
Blue, you're just lonely.

324
00:36:37,754 --> 00:36:39,755
[Literature Exhibition: Romeo and Juliet]

325
00:37:25,240 --> 00:37:26,610
♪ To you ♪

326
00:37:28,759 --> 00:37:30,850
♪ The one who means everything to me ♪

327
00:37:32,850 --> 00:37:34,330
I heard your dad’s such a big shot?

328
00:37:35,770 --> 00:37:38,471
Don’t forget, he’s not the one sitting in class.

329
00:37:38,860 --> 00:37:41,810
♪ Our dream seemed within reach ♪

330
00:37:42,608 --> 00:37:44,090
♪ But you ♪

331
00:37:46,250 --> 00:37:50,010
- ♪ slowly faded away and changed ♪
- I asked you--

332
00:37:50,525 --> 00:37:51,526
what’s the filling?

333
00:37:53,357 --> 00:37:54,970
Good...feelings.

334
00:38:00,746 --> 00:38:02,010
Fine. Good feelings it is.

335
00:38:04,746 --> 00:38:06,610
♪ I’ll be waiting ♪

336
00:38:07,189 --> 00:38:09,810
♪ Though it may be only a dream ♪

337
00:38:10,482 --> 00:38:14,850
♪ Of a better day ♪

338
00:38:15,661 --> 00:38:18,450
♪ When you return to me ♪

339
00:38:18,970 --> 00:38:22,930
♪ There’ll be love and everything we need ♪

340
00:38:23,309 --> 00:38:27,250
♪ There’ll be dreams at the end of the road ♪

341
00:38:27,698 --> 00:38:30,210
♪ You’re the one who made my love... ♪

342
00:38:33,150 --> 00:38:34,930
♪ become real ♪

343
00:38:38,661 --> 00:38:40,250
Do we really need to make such a big deal out of this?

344
00:38:40,781 --> 00:38:41,970
It’s only movie night.

345
00:38:42,518 --> 00:38:45,965
Damn right I’m serious.

346
00:38:46,082 --> 00:38:47,330
We dorm kids only get to go out on weekends.

347
00:38:48,167 --> 00:38:50,610
Stop sitting around and help me pick out an outfit.

348
00:38:54,600 --> 00:38:56,510
- Ugh!
- You think it's cute?

349
00:38:58,893 --> 00:39:00,830
Which one do you think? I think it's this one.

350
00:39:01,293 --> 00:39:02,570
- Yeah.
- Right? I think so.

351
00:39:02,810 --> 00:39:03,811
The color suits me better.

352
00:39:05,069 --> 00:39:06,070
Phakjira,

353
00:39:06,400 --> 00:39:08,602
you can't join the movie night tonight.

354
00:39:09,008 --> 00:39:10,610
You will be in detention.

355
00:39:11,170 --> 00:39:13,290
Your PE teacher told me

356
00:39:13,351 --> 00:39:15,210
you’re still on probation for what you did in class.

357
00:39:16,256 --> 00:39:19,130
What do you mean? She said she'd let it slide.

358
00:39:19,466 --> 00:39:22,816
If she has to serve detention, can it at least be on another day?

359
00:39:23,946 --> 00:39:27,170
Phakjira, you are forbidden from attending movie night tonight.

360
00:39:27,610 --> 00:39:29,670
As punishment for wearing inappropriate attire in PE class,

361
00:39:29,840 --> 00:39:31,210
you will be confined to the dorm.

362
00:39:31,370 --> 00:39:34,277
You must also write a reflection essay and submit it to me tomorrow morning.

363
00:39:34,371 --> 00:39:35,690
No arguments.

364
00:40:24,034 --> 00:40:25,130
I like the lights.

365
00:40:26,310 --> 00:40:27,210
Tokyo.

366
00:40:27,296 --> 00:40:29,097
More people showed up than I thought.

367
00:40:51,232 --> 00:40:52,630
How long have you been here?

368
00:40:52,690 --> 00:40:53,691
For a while now.

369
00:40:55,306 --> 00:40:57,770
Blue can’t join us. Our PE teacher wouldn’t let it slide,

370
00:40:58,240 --> 00:40:59,730
so she’s in detention.

371
00:41:00,554 --> 00:41:01,555
Wait, are you serious?

372
00:41:01,760 --> 00:41:03,360
I'm dead serious.

373
00:41:03,890 --> 00:41:05,250
I feel bad for her though.

374
00:41:05,319 --> 00:41:07,330
She’s all alone in the detention room.

375
00:41:08,970 --> 00:41:10,850
Forget it. Let’s head over there instead.

376
00:41:11,784 --> 00:41:12,785
Is  this good?

377
00:41:16,437 --> 00:41:17,438
Tokyo?

378
00:41:18,368 --> 00:41:19,369
Yeah?

379
00:41:20,021 --> 00:41:21,022
Where are you going?

380
00:41:21,770 --> 00:41:24,410
I need to use a bathroom. I'll be right back.

381
00:41:25,370 --> 00:41:26,371
I'll catch up with you later.

382
00:42:11,410 --> 00:42:13,211
[STAFF ONLY. NO UNAUTHORIZED ENTRY]

383
00:43:35,357 --> 00:43:36,358
How did you get here?

384
00:43:37,562 --> 00:43:39,573
I climbed the ladder.

385
00:43:41,183 --> 00:43:42,184
What?

386
00:43:45,408 --> 00:43:48,370
I need to talk to you.

387
00:43:49,866 --> 00:43:50,867
Right now?

388
00:43:51,829 --> 00:43:53,650
We’ll see each other tomorrow.

389
00:43:55,456 --> 00:43:56,457
No!

390
00:43:56,874 --> 00:43:58,890
I need to talk to you now.

391
00:44:00,012 --> 00:44:03,410
Okay, hurry up and say it.

392
00:44:04,037 --> 00:44:05,338
This is very dangerous for both of us.

393
00:44:07,610 --> 00:44:08,611
Okay.

394
00:44:14,178 --> 00:44:15,450
I…

395
00:44:16,189 --> 00:44:17,770
I…

396
00:44:19,757 --> 00:44:21,530
I think…

397
00:44:25,530 --> 00:44:26,810
I think I li...

398
00:44:29,168 --> 00:44:30,169
What?

399
00:44:36,968 --> 00:44:39,485
Why don't you tell me tomorrow? Okay?

400
00:44:40,961 --> 00:44:41,962
I…

401
00:44:44,090 --> 00:44:45,618
I think I like you, Blue.

402
00:44:51,682 --> 00:44:52,683
Yeah.

403
00:44:55,117 --> 00:44:57,293
I’m not sure

404
00:44:57,608 --> 00:44:58,669
what to call this feeling.

405
00:44:59,565 --> 00:45:02,392
I don't know if it's a crush.

406
00:45:03,496 --> 00:45:05,250
All I know is that

407
00:45:07,008 --> 00:45:09,800
whenever I’m with you,

408
00:45:11,429 --> 00:45:12,430
my heart never stops racing.

409
00:45:13,120 --> 00:45:15,290
And I never want our time together

410
00:45:15,562 --> 00:45:16,563
to end.

411
00:45:21,693 --> 00:45:23,210
So… I think I’ve fallen for you, Blue.

412
00:45:30,496 --> 00:45:31,497
But…

413
00:45:35,210 --> 00:45:37,911
if you don’t feel the same way,

414
00:45:38,829 --> 00:45:39,830
that’s okay.

415
00:45:42,178 --> 00:45:43,179
I just felt like

416
00:45:46,466 --> 00:45:47,467
I…

417
00:45:48,274 --> 00:45:49,275
needed…

418
00:45:49,800 --> 00:45:52,621
to be honest with you about my feelings.

419
00:46:05,634 --> 00:46:06,635
Well,

420
00:46:07,805 --> 00:46:09,250
I should go.

421
00:46:11,874 --> 00:46:13,170
See you tomorrow.

422
00:46:16,509 --> 00:46:17,510
Bye.

423
00:47:01,160 --> 00:47:03,130
I’m a Kongpurim.

424
00:47:03,282 --> 00:47:05,290
There’s no way I’d get involved with a Monchaitrakul.

425
00:47:29,950 --> 00:47:30,951
No!

426
00:47:31,530 --> 00:47:33,810
I’m friends with a Kongpurim. So what, Dad?

427
00:47:34,346 --> 00:47:35,347
Blue!

428
00:47:36,986 --> 00:47:39,930
You said it was grown-up business, didn’t you?

429
00:47:40,997 --> 00:47:42,810
So whatever feud exists between our families

430
00:47:42,830 --> 00:47:43,992
has nothing to do with a kid like me.

431
00:48:21,125 --> 00:48:23,290
- [Next Episode Preview]
- If our families find out about us,

432
00:48:23,413 --> 00:48:25,297
there’ll definitely be a civil war.

433
00:48:25,674 --> 00:48:27,890
Let's just keep it between us.

434
00:48:29,826 --> 00:48:30,827
Are you dating someone?

435
00:48:31,469 --> 00:48:33,890
Do you really think two people from rival mafia families in this province

436
00:48:33,997 --> 00:48:35,330
could ever make a relationship work?

437
00:48:35,485 --> 00:48:36,650
You think it's gonna last?

438
00:48:37,450 --> 00:48:39,890
All our distributors have pulled out of their transportation deals with us.

439
00:48:40,173 --> 00:48:41,970
You can’t let them disrespect us like this, Dad.

440
00:48:42,690 --> 00:48:45,730
Why don't you meet up with their daughter?

